# =============================================================================
# 10-base.list.chroot - NimbusOS base system (required)
# =============================================================================
# What: system basics, networking, audio and Mesa that NimbusOS needs to work.
# Why:  spec section 1. The kernel is added by live-build itself
#       (lb config --linux-flavours). Firmware, microcode and optional tools
#       are in 15-firmware and 25-desktop-extras, which nimbusos-desktop only
#       Recommends (docs/PLAN.md NOTE-48).
#
# Format rules for every list in this directory (live-build 1:20250505 passes
# the file through printf and runs lines that start with an exclamation mark):
#   * one package name per line, plain comment lines starting with a hash;
#   * no comment after a package name, no percent sign, no backslash.
# A header line "#! nimbus: <role>" sets how nimbusos-desktop lists the
# packages: no marker = Depends, desktop-recommends = Recommends,
# exclude-from-desktop = not listed. tools/verify-trixie.sh enforces the
# format and proves every package exists in Trixie. Every package in a list is
# installed in the image; through nimbusos-desktop, a package added here also
# reaches installed systems with their next update.
# =============================================================================

# System basics
sudo
locales
console-setup
keyboard-configuration
ca-certificates
cryptsetup
systemd-timesyncd
unattended-upgrades

# Networking
network-manager

# Audio (PipeWire with WirePlumber)
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
wireplumber

# Graphics: Mesa OpenGL, Vulkan and VA-API drivers
libgl1-mesa-dri
mesa-vulkan-drivers
mesa-va-drivers

# Boot splash (the theme ships in nimbusos-branding)
plymouth
